			"Message": "docs(LICENSE): Migrate from CC0 to Land Public License v1.0\n\nReplaced CC0 1.0 Universal public domain dedication with new Land Public License (LPL v1.0) to establish clear copyleft terms for the Land code editor project. This change:\n- Implements strong copyleft for Land components while allowing combination with External Works under different licenses\n- Adds patent grants and defensive termination clauses to protect contributors\n- Defines compatibility rules for integration with GPLv3+/AGPLv3+/MPL2.0 projects\n- Maintains source availability requirements aligned with Land's open collaboration goals\n- Establishes Sofia, Bulgaria as governing jurisdiction for disputes\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: Changes license terms from public domain to reciprocal copyleft. All contributors and users must now comply with LPL's distribution terms including source code provision and compatibility requirements.",
